---This corresponds to an in-toto link.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Link
---@field command? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.StringList This field contains the full command executed for the step. This can also be empty if links are generated for operations that aren't directly mapped to a specific command. Each term in the command is an independent string in the list. An example of a command in the in-toto metadata field is: "command": ["git", "clone", "https://github.com/in-toto/demo-project.git"]
---@field materials? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.GrafeasV1beta1IntotoArtifactList Materials are the supply chain artifacts that go into the step and are used for the operation performed. The key of the map is the path of the artifact and the structure contains the recorded hash information. An example is: "materials": [ { "resource_uri": "foo/bar", "hashes": { "sha256": "ebebf...", : } } ]
---@field products? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.GrafeasV1beta1IntotoArtifactList Products are the supply chain artifacts generated as a result of the step. The structure is identical to that of materials.
---@field byproducts? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.ByProducts ByProducts are data generated as part of a software supply chain step, but are not the actual result of the step.
---@field environment? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Environment This is a field that can be used to capture information about the environment. It is suggested for this field to contain information that details environment variables, filesystem information, and the present working directory. The recommended structure of this field is: "environment": { "custom_values": { "variables": "", "filesystem": "", "workdir": "", "": "..." } }

---Response for listing occurrences for a note.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.ListNoteOccurrencesResponse
---@field occurrences? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.OccurrenceList The occurrences attached to the specified note.
---@field nextPageToken? string Token to provide to skip to a particular spot in the list.

---Response for listing notes.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.ListNotesResponse
---@field unreachable? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.StringList Unordered list. Unreachable regions. Populated for requests from the global region when `return_partial_success` is set. Format: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/locations/[LOCATION]`
---@field notes? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.NoteList The notes requested.
---@field nextPageToken? string The next pagination token in the list response. It should be used as `page_token` for the following request. An empty value means no more results.

