---Version contains structured information about the version of a package.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Version
---@field inclusive? boolean Whether this version is specifying part of an inclusive range. Grafeas does not have the capability to specify version ranges; instead we have fields that specify start version and end versions. At times this is insufficient - we also need to specify whether the version is included in the range or is excluded from the range. This boolean is expected to be set to true when the version is included in a range.
---@field kind? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VersionKindEnum|string Required. Distinguishes between sentinel MIN/MAX versions and normal versions.
---@field revision? string The iteration of the package build from the above version.
---@field epoch? number Used to correct mistakes in the version numbering scheme.
---@field name? string Required only when version kind is NORMAL. The main part of the version name.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VersionKindEnum "VERSION_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"NORMAL"|"MINIMUM"|"MAXIMUM"

---VexAssessment provides all publisher provided Vex information that is related to this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VexAssessment
---@field remediations? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.RemediationList Specifies details on how to handle (and presumably, fix) a vulnerability.
---@field cve? string Holds the MITRE standard Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) tracking number for the vulnerability. Deprecated: Use vulnerability_id instead to denote CVEs.
---@field relatedUris? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.RelatedUrlList Holds a list of references associated with this vulnerability item and assessment.
---@field justification? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Justification Justification provides the justification when the state of the assessment if NOT_AFFECTED.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VexAssessmentStateEnum|string Provides the state of this Vulnerability assessment.
---@field vulnerabilityId? string The vulnerability identifier for this Assessment. Will hold one of common identifiers e.g. CVE, GHSA etc.
---@field impacts? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.StringList Contains information about the impact of this vulnerability, this will change with time.
---@field noteName? string The VulnerabilityAssessment note from which this VexAssessment was generated. This will be of the form: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/notes/[NOTE_ID]`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VexAssessmentStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"AFFECTED"|"NOT_AFFECTED"|"FIXED"|"UNDER_INVESTIGATION"

---Vulnerability provides metadata about a security vulnerability in a Note.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Vulnerability
---@field severity? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilitySeverityEnum|string Note provider assigned impact of the vulnerability.
---@field details? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.DetailList All information about the package to specifically identify this vulnerability. One entry per (version range and cpe_uri) the package vulnerability has manifested in.
---@field cvssScore? number The CVSS score for this vulnerability.
---@field windowsDetails? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WindowsDetailList Windows details get their own format because the information format and model don't match a normal detail. Specifically Windows updates are done as patches, thus Windows vulnerabilities really are a missing package, rather than a package being at an incorrect version.
---@field advisoryPublishTime? string The time this advisory was published by the source.
---@field cvssV3? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.CVSSv3 The full description of the CVSS for version 3.
---@field cvssVersion? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilityCvssVersionEnum|string CVSS version used to populate cvss_score and severity.
---@field cvssV4? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.CVSS The full description of the CVSS for version 4.
---@field cvssV2? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.CVSS The full description of the CVSS for version 2.
---@field sourceUpdateTime? string The time this information was last changed at the source. This is an upstream timestamp from the underlying information source - e.g. Ubuntu security tracker.
---@field cwe? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.StringList A list of CWE for this vulnerability. For details, see: https://cwe.mitre.org/index.html

---A single VulnerabilityAssessmentNote represents one particular product's vulnerability assessment for one CVE.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilityAssessmentNote
---@field product? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Product The product affected by this vex.
---@field longDescription? string A detailed description of this Vex.
---@field languageCode? string Identifies the language used by this document, corresponding to IETF BCP 47 / RFC 5646.
---@field publisher? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Publisher Publisher details of this Note.
---@field assessment? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Assessment Represents a vulnerability assessment for the product.
---@field title? string The title of the note. E.g. `Vex-Debian-11.4`
---@field shortDescription? string A one sentence description of this Vex.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilityCvssVersionEnum "CVSS_VERSION_UNSPECIFIED"|"CVSS_VERSION_2"|"CVSS_VERSION_3"|"CVSS_VERSION_4"

---The location of the vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilityLocation
---@field package? string Required. The package being described.
---@field version? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.Version Required. The version of the package being described.
---@field cpeUri? string Required. The CPE URI in [cpe format](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) format. Examples include distro or storage location for vulnerable jar.

---A summary of how many vulnerability occurrences there are per resource and severity type.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilityOccurrencesSummary
---@field counts? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.FixableTotalByDigestList A listing by resource of the number of fixable and total vulnerabilities.
---@field unreachable? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.StringList Unordered list. Unreachable regions. Populated for requests from the global region when `return_partial_success` is set. Format: `projects/[PROJECT_ID]/locations/[LOCATION]`

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.VulnerabilitySeverityEnum "SEVERITY_UNSPECIFIED"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WindowsDetail
---@field name? string Required. The name of the vulnerability.
---@field description? string The description of the vulnerability.
---@field fixingKbs? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.KnowledgeBaseList Required. The names of the KBs which have hotfixes to mitigate this vulnerability. Note that there may be multiple hotfixes (and thus multiple KBs) that mitigate a given vulnerability. Currently any listed kb's presence is considered a fix.
---@field cpeUri? string Required. The CPE URI in [cpe format](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) in which the vulnerability manifests. Examples include distro or storage location for vulnerable jar.

---@alias gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WindowsDetailList gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WindowsDetail[]

---Result of Workspace Policy scan.
---@class gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WorkspacePolicyResult
---@field verdict? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WorkspacePolicyResultVerdictEnum|string Verdict of the scan.
---@field scanStatus? gcp.unstable.containeranalysis_v1beta1.WorkspacePolicyResultScanStatusEnum|string Status of the scan.

